{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3530","id":4727202489,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABGcNiuQ","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3530","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3530.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3530.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3530","number":3530,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"state: send relogin of an expired node as a whole node","user":{"login":"nextsux","id":926250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjI1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/926250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux","html_url":"https://github.com/nextsux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nextsux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\r\n\r\n- I'm using OIDC flow for our VPN and users are required by policy to\r\n  use 2FA every time they connect after some time. So I use expiration\r\n  on their clients that forces them to go through OIDC login flow again\r\n  where I can enforce any MFA/password policy we require.\r\n- The issue is that when user reauthenticates itself, their traffic does\r\n  not go through tailnet until they restart tailscaled.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n- After a node's key expires and the user re-authenticates (web/OIDC\r\n  `tailscale up`, or a pre-auth key), the node gets a new node key and\r\n  reaches Running, but peers drop all its WireGuard traffic.\r\n- Disco keeps working (`tailscale ping` gets pongs, peers log `now using`),\r\n  but TSMP/ICMP time out and `LastHandshake` stays zero.\r\n- It recovers only after `tailscaled` restarts on the node, or Headscale\r\n  restarts.\r\n\r\n## Cause\r\n\r\n- Peers get the expired node as a whole node with `Expired: true`.\r\n- The relogin goes out as `change.NodeKeyRotated`, a `tailcfg.PeerChange`\r\n  patch (Key, DiscoKey, KeyExpiry, Endpoints).\r\n- `PeerChange` has no `Expired` field, and the client's patch path leaves\r\n  it as it is, so peers keep the node expired.\r\n- The Tailscale client gives an expired peer no AllowedIPs\r\n  (`routemanager.peerViewOf`), so wireguard-go does not create the lazy\r\n  peer and drops its handshakes.\r\n- Why it doesn't happen on every relogin: if the first MapRequest after\r\n  the relogin changes peer-visible Hostinfo, `buildMapRequestChangeResponse`\r\n  sends the whole node anyway and the flag clears. This is what happens\r\n  when the client registers without its peerapi services and adds them\r\n  once Running.\r\n- It shows up when the expired client has settled before the user logs\r\n  in again: it keeps its netmap and serves peerapi again while in\r\n  NeedsLogin (seen with 1.98 and newer; not with 1.84), so it registers\r\n  with the same Hostinfo it later reports, and nothing ever clears the\r\n  flag.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\n- `reauthChange` now gets `wasExpired`. If the node was expired before\r\n  the relogin, the relogin is sent as `change.NodeAdded` instead of the\r\n  key-rotation patch.\r\n- This covers both `HandleNodeFromAuthPath` and `HandleNodeFromPreAuthKey`.\r\n- Relogins of non-expired nodes keep the patch path.\r\n- I checked the other paths that can make a node non-expired:\r\n  `SetNodeExpiry` and new registrations already send the whole node, and\r\n  a MapRequest can't change expiry.\r\n- Fix was co-authored with LLM, hand checked by me.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nAll of these fail without the fix and pass with it:\r\n\r\n- Integration: `TestAuthWebFlowReloginExpiredNode`. For each client, it\r\n  expires one node, waits until the client is in NeedsLogin with peerapi\r\n  serving again, then logs it back in via the web flow. It checks that\r\n  every peer sees the new key with `Expired=false` and gets a TSMP pong\r\n  from it. Clients older than 1.98 are skipped as the relogged node\r\n  because they don't serve peerapi while expired, so their relogin always\r\n  changes Hostinfo; they still take part as peers.\r\n  - Without the fix: 1.102, 1.98, head and unstable fail on the expired\r\n    flag and the TSMP ping.\r\n- servertest: `TestReloginOfExpiredNodeClearsPeerExpiry`. A deterministic\r\n  version using a real `controlclient.Direct` with fixed Hostinfo.\r\n- `TestHandleNodeFromAuthPath_ReloginOfExpiredNode`: the interactive path\r\n  returns a whole-node change when the node was expired, and a patch when\r\n  it was not.\r\n- `TestReauthChange` extended with the expired case.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the CONTRIBUTING.md file\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [x] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed  <!-- not needed -->\r\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:16:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T14:17:26Z","closed_at":"2026-10-03T14:17:26Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"24bfa17a9dcb2ffe3dc0ac734a5d90e514a71843","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/